t1 = conv2d_transpose(input_tensor)# Apply pointwise transposed convolution to the input tensor. This includes: an optional stride and dilation factor, a valid padding (default), and optionally output padding that results in output dimensions that are divisible by the provided stride (default 0). If True, then the output height and width are calculated as: output_height = ceil(input_height / stride) - 1 output_width = ceil(input_width / stride) - 1. In other words, the default calculation of the output size works for stride 2. Otherwise, it is set to zero at both ends of the convolution operation by adding zeros (if padding mode is "constant") or by setting to max(kernelsize, stride). Note that specifying the stride and dilation factor may result in input and output tensors being not aligned as per standard conv2d implementation.
